# CLAUDE.md — AI Contributor Guide

Rules, patterns and constraints for any AI agent contributing to **{{ project_name }}**.
Only the non-negotiable lives here. Detail lives in `.claude/rules/` (loaded by path),
procedures in `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, decisions in `docs/decisions/`, and
what the agent may do alone in `AUTONOMY.md` + `.claude/autonomy.json`. The hooks in
`.claude/hooks/` enforce the gates below; a hook refusal is a rule, not a bug to work around.

---

{% if has_pipeline %}
## 00. QA workflow — driving a ticket

The agent drives tickets by reconstructing state from live artifacts, then spawning the
sub-agent for the missing phase. **The live artifacts are the state.** Full procedure:
`.claude/rules/pipeline.md`. The ticket key (`{{ tracker_project_key }}-NNNN`) is the join key in every artifact.

### Phase-derivation table — walk it top to bottom, every time

| Probe | Finding | Next action |
|---|---|---|
| `qa/dossiers/<KEY>.md` | None found | Run `ticket-intake` skill Step 2 (dossier) — no sub-agent before it exists |
| Dossier | No Acceptance Criteria and nothing found outside them | Halt → escalate to human{% if has_comm_platform %} via {{ comm_platform_label }}{% endif %} |
| {{ doc_label }} TD doc (key in title) | None found | Spawn **test-design-agent** |
| TD doc | Status = *In Review* | Spawn **bdd-agent** |
| TD doc | Status = *Approved* | Continue to test repo probe |
{% if has_test_repo %}
| {{ test_repo_label }} (Refs = key) | Approved TD but no cases | Spawn **bdd-agent** |
| {{ test_repo_label }} | Cases exist, no run / results | Spawn **manual-agent** |
| {{ test_repo_label }} run | All cases have results | Continue to automation probe |
| `automation-coverage.md` / spec tags | ≥1 automatable case with no spec tag | Spawn **automation-agent** |
| `automation-coverage.md` / spec tags | No pending rows | **Done** → final compliance score |
{% endif %}

Sub-agents run serially, carry the handoff contract (`handoff-protocol` skill), and are
checked by the `convention-check` skill after each return; three rewrites of one phase
escalate to a human.

{% else %}
## 00. Ticket intake — mandatory order of actions

When anyone hands over a ticket to test, verify, QA, or automate — invoke the
`ticket-intake` skill and follow it. The order is not optional:

```
1. Track     open the sprint AI-usage record (scripts/qa_track.py)
2. Dossier   read the WHOLE ticket — comments, attachments, PRs, linked tickets — into qa/dossiers/<KEY>.md
3. Inventory do the cases already exist? Check local specs AND {{ doc_label }}
4. Author    write the missing Gherkin cases as a draft
5. APPROVE   the QA engineer approves the cases — nothing runs before this
6. Execute   dev first, then staging, with evidence
7. Automate  only cases that passed
8. Sync      {{ doc_label }}, Coverage Stats, task tracker
```

Three hard gates:

- **Never author cases from the ticket description alone** (step 2). Comments, PRs and
  attachments change scope; a link you cannot fetch is `NOT FOUND`, never guessed.
- **Never execute test cases that were not approved** (step 5).
- **Never close a task without the Coverage Stats sync** (step 8) when any case was
  created or automated.

